      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, these are a good start, but question 3 got cut off. also, i noticed the score for this set was pretty low on our tracker because none of the specific theme-words actually showed up in the questions themselves. \n\ncan you finish the list and give me 5 complete questions? try to make sure the core themes are clearly represented in the questions so the score is higher, but i'm still stressing—please don't just force the words in a way that sounds fake. they need to sound like something a real recruiter would actually ask.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll provide the complete question 3 and draft two new questions to meet the \"innovation\" and \"collaboration\" themes. Here is the complete list:\n\n1. \"Tell me about a time when you identified a process or technology gap in your previous role, and how you proposed and implemented a creative solution to address it. How did your team respond to your idea, and what was the outcome?\"\n\nThis question assesses the candidate's ability to innovate and take initiative, as well as their collaboration skills in presenting and implementing their ideas.\n\n2. \"Describe a situation where you had to adapt an existing project or process to meet the changing needs of your team or organization. What steps did you take to ensure a smooth transition, and what benefits did the team realize from the changes?\"\n\nThis question evaluates the candidate's ability to innovate, collaborate, and navigate change, all while maintaining a focus on the team's needs and goals.\n\n3. \"Can you share an experience where you had to balance competing priorities and stakeholder demands within a team project? How did you facilitate open communication, and what strategies did you use to build consensus and drive the project forward?\"\n\nThis question assesses the candidate's collaboration skills, such as communication, delegation,",
